{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Explore taxonomy RDF — local SPARQL queries\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses `rdflib` to load the generated TTL bundles locally and run SPARQL queries interactively.  \n",
    "No server required — edit queries in-place and re-run cells.\n",
    "\n",
    "Once a query looks good, copy it to **[SPARQLQueries](https://github.com/pathway-lod/SPARQLQueries)** and add it to **[Snorql-UI](https://github.com/pathway-lod/Snorql-UI)**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Kernel:** select `plantmetwiki-rdf` (register once with `python -m ipykernel install --user --name plantmetwiki-rdf`).\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## ⚠️ Limitations — read before writing queries\n",
    "\n",
    "`rdflib` is a pure-Python in-memory SPARQL engine with **no query optimizer**. Keep queries simple:\n",
    "\n",
    "| ✅ Works well | ❌ Avoid |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Simple `SELECT` with 1–2 triple patterns | Cartesian products (`?a` × `?b` with no shared variable) |\n",
    "| `COUNT` / `GROUP BY` on one variable | `FILTER(STRSTARTS(?a, STR(?b)))` over large sets — O(n²), very slow |\n",
    "| Queries on the small bundles (~4–160 MB) | Loading the 300 MB core bundle (minutes + several GB RAM) |\n",
    "| Single-bundle queries | Cross-bundle joins (taxonomy + core together) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**URI structure:**\n",
    "```\n",
    "Pathway:  http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/pathways/PC1_r<version>\n",
    "DataNode: http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/Pathway/PC1_r<version>/DataNode/<id>\n",
    "```\n",
    "Both the taxonomy-extra and properties-extra bundles use **the same URIs**, so they are implicitly linked by shared subject — no explicit `owl:sameAs` needed.\n",
    "\n",
    "**For cross-layer queries** (e.g. "which pathway contains which species"), use the **Virtuoso** production endpoint where `wp:isPartOf` links DataNodes to their pathway across both graphs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from rdflib import Graph, Namespace\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "WP     = Namespace(\"http://vocabularies.wikipathways.org/wp#\")\n",
    "NCBI   = Namespace(\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_\")\n",
    "PMW    = Namespace(\"http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/vocab/\")\n",
    "DCTERMS = Namespace(\"http://purl.org/dc/terms/\")\n",
    "\n",
    "PREFIXES = \"\"\"\n",
    "PREFIX wp:      <http://vocabularies.wikipathways.org/wp#>\n",
    "PREFIX ncbi:    <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_>\n",
    "PREFIX pmw:     <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/vocab/>\n",
    "PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>\n",
    "PREFIX rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "def sparql(g: Graph, query: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Run a SPARQL SELECT and return a DataFrame.\"\"\"\n",
    "    results = g.query(PREFIXES + query)\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(results, columns=[str(v) for v in results.vars])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Ready.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load bundles\n",
    "\n",
    "Both files contain exclusively `wp:organism` / `pmw:gpmlProperty` statements linked to **the same pathway URIs** — no separate join needed.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Bundle | Size | Content |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `all_gpml_taxonomy_extra-*.ttl` | ~4 MB | `wp:organism` triples only |\n",
    "| `all_gpml_properties_extra-*.ttl` | ~160 MB | PlantCyc key-value properties as blank nodes |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "VERSION = \"plantcyc17.0.0-gpml2021\"\n",
    "bundles_dir = Path(\"../output/bundles\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Taxonomy extra — small, fast\n",
    "print(\"Loading taxonomy extra...\")\n",
    "g_tax = Graph()\n",
    "g_tax.parse(str(bundles_dir / f\"all_gpml_taxonomy_extra-{VERSION}.ttl\"), format=\"turtle\")\n",
    "print(f\"  {len(g_tax):,} triples  (all wp:organism statements)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Properties extra — larger, ~1 min\n",
    "print(\"Loading properties extra...\")\n",
    "g_prop = Graph()\n",
    "g_prop.parse(str(bundles_dir / f\"all_gpml_properties_extra-{VERSION}.ttl\"), format=\"turtle\")\n",
    "print(f\"  {len(g_prop):,} triples  (all pmw:gpmlProperty + pmw:plantcycId + dcterms:identifier)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. Pathway IRIs and PlantCyc IDs\n",
    "\n",
    "Each pathway has:\n",
    "- A **stable IRI** in the form `http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/pathways/PC{n}_r{version}`\n",
    "- A **PlantCyc ID** (e.g. `PWY-6933`) stored as `pmw:plantcycId` and `dcterms:identifier`\n",
    "- A **source link** to `https://identifiers.org/plantcyc/{id}`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pathway IRI + PlantCyc ID + identifiers.org link — sample 10\n",
    "sparql(g_prop, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?pathway_iri ?plantcyc_id ?source\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?pathway_iri pmw:plantcycId ?plantcyc_id .\n",
    "    ?pathway_iri dcterms:source ?source .\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?pathway_iri), \"/pathways/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Total number of pathway IRIs with a PlantCyc ID\n",
    "sparql(g_prop, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?pathway_iri) AS ?pathways_with_plantcyc_id)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?pathway_iri pmw:plantcycId ?id .\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?pathway_iri), \"/pathways/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 2. Verify taxonomy and properties are linked to the same IRIs\n",
    "\n",
    "Since both bundles use the same pathway IRI as subject, loading them together means the same URI gets triples from both — no explicit link needed. Let's confirm a few pathways appear in both."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Merge into one graph to query across both bundles\n",
    "g_both = g_tax + g_prop\n",
    "print(f\"Combined graph: {len(g_both):,} triples\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pathways that appear in BOTH taxonomy extra (wp:organism) AND properties extra (pmw:plantcycId)\n",
    "# These should be all 1162 pathways\n",
    "sparql(g_both, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?pathway) AS ?pathways_in_both_bundles)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?pathway wp:organism ncbi:33090 .     # from taxonomy extra\n",
    "    ?pathway pmw:plantcycId ?id .         # from properties extra\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?pathway), \"/pathways/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sample: pathway IRI + PlantCyc ID + Viridiplantae annotation together\n",
    "sparql(g_both, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?pathway_iri ?plantcyc_id ?organism\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?pathway_iri pmw:plantcycId  ?plantcyc_id .\n",
    "    ?pathway_iri wp:organism     ?organism .\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?pathway_iri), \"/pathways/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Explore GPML properties\n",
    "\n",
    "All `<Property key=\"...\" value=\"...\">` elements from the GPML are stored as blank nodes:\n",
    "```turtle\n",
    "?subject pmw:gpmlProperty [ pmw:key \"...\"; pmw:value \"...\" ] .\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# All unique property keys and how often they appear — top 20\n",
    "sparql(g_prop, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?key (COUNT(?key) AS ?count)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?subject pmw:gpmlProperty ?bn .\n",
    "    ?bn pmw:key ?key .\n",
    "}\n",
    "GROUP BY ?key\n",
    "ORDER BY DESC(?count)\n",
    "LIMIT 20\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Original per-pathway species list — stored as Property key='Organism'\n",
    "# This is the original multi-species string preserved from PlantCyc,\n",
    "# now that the GPML organism attribute only carries Viridiplantae\n",
    "sparql(g_prop, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?pathway_iri ?original_species\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?pathway_iri pmw:gpmlProperty ?bn .\n",
    "    ?bn pmw:key   \"Organism\" ;\n",
    "        pmw:value ?original_species .\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?pathway_iri), \"/pathways/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# DataNode properties — sample UniqueID values for genes\n",
    "sparql(g_prop, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?datanode ?plantcyc_id\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?datanode pmw:gpmlProperty ?bn .\n",
    "    ?bn pmw:key   \"UniqueID\" ;\n",
    "        pmw:value ?plantcyc_id .\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?datanode), \"/DataNode/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Taxonomy-level: Viridiplantae coverage\n",
    "\n",
    "Every pathway and reaction should carry `wp:organism ncbi:33090`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# How many distinct pathway/reaction URIs have wp:organism ncbi:33090?\n",
    "# Expected: 2478 (1162 pathways + 1316 reactions)\n",
    "sparql(g_tax, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?resource) AS ?resources_with_viridiplantae)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?resource wp:organism ncbi:33090 .\n",
    "}\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Species distribution across DataNode URIs — top 20\n",
    "sparql(g_tax, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?species (COUNT(DISTINCT ?node) AS ?node_count)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?node wp:organism ?species .\n",
    "    FILTER(?species != ncbi:33090)\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?node), \"/DataNode/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "GROUP BY ?species\n",
    "ORDER BY DESC(?node_count)\n",
    "LIMIT 20\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sample DataNode URIs annotated with Arabidopsis thaliana (ncbi:3702)\n",
    "sparql(g_tax, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?node\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?node wp:organism ncbi:3702 .\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?node), \"/DataNode/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Cross-layer queries → use Virtuoso\n",
    "\n",
    "Queries joining taxonomy + core WikiPathways RDF (e.g. "which pathway contains which species?") require `wp:isPartOf` which lives in the core bundle.  \n",
    "Run these on the **Virtuoso production endpoint** using named graphs:\n",
    "\n",
    "```sparql\n",
    "# Pathways containing at least one Arabidopsis thaliana node\n",
    "PREFIX wp:   <http://vocabularies.wikipathways.org/wp#>\n",
    "PREFIX ncbi: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_>\n",
    "\n",
    "SELECT ?pathway (COUNT(DISTINCT ?node) AS ?arabidopsis_nodes)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "  GRAPH <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/graph/pathways> {\n",
    "      ?node wp:isPartOf ?pathway .\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  GRAPH <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/graph/gpml-taxonomy-extra> {\n",
    "      ?node wp:organism ncbi:3702 .\n",
    "  }\n",
    "}\n",
    "GROUP BY ?pathway\n",
    "ORDER BY DESC(?arabidopsis_nodes)\n",
    "LIMIT 20\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "```sparql\n",
    "# Pathway IRI + PlantCyc ID + species annotation in one query\n",
    "PREFIX wp:      <http://vocabularies.wikipathways.org/wp#>\n",
    "PREFIX ncbi:    <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_>\n",
    "PREFIX pmw:     <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/vocab/>\n",
    "\n",
    "SELECT ?pathway_iri ?plantcyc_id ?organism\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "  GRAPH <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/graph/gpml-properties-extra> {\n",
    "      ?pathway_iri pmw:plantcycId ?plantcyc_id .\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  GRAPH <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/graph/gpml-taxonomy-extra> {\n",
    "      ?pathway_iri wp:organism ?organism .\n",
    "  }\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 20\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 6. Sandbox — write your own queries here\n",
    "\n",
    "Use `g_tax`, `g_prop`, or `g_both`. When a query is validated, copy it to **[SPARQLQueries](https://github.com/pathway-lod/SPARQLQueries)**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sparql(g_both, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT *\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    # ← write your query here\n",
    "    # available graphs: g_tax (taxonomy), g_prop (properties), g_both (merged)\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 20\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  }
